# 🎯 Linear Discriminant Analysis (LDA)

## 📖 Overview

Linear Discriminant Analysis (LDA) is a supervised dimensionality reduction technique used to reduce the number of features while maximizing the separation between different classes.

LDA uses class labels while finding the most useful directions for separating the data.

---

## 🎯 Objective

The objective of this project is to:

* Understand Linear Discriminant Analysis.
* Apply LDA to a real-world dataset.
* Standardize numerical features.
* Reduce the dimensionality of the dataset.
* Maximize class separability.
* Visualize the transformed data.

---

## 🧠 What is LDA?

LDA finds linear combinations of features that maximize the separation between different classes while minimizing the variation within each class.

Unlike PCA, LDA uses the target labels during dimensionality reduction.

---

## ⚖️ PCA vs LDA

| PCA                                         | LDA                                                        |
| ------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |
| Unsupervised                                | Supervised                                                 |
| Does not use target labels                  | Uses target labels                                         |
| Maximizes variance                          | Maximizes class separation                                 |
| Useful for general dimensionality reduction | Useful for classification-related dimensionality reduction |

